Purpose
=======

This file tells LLM agents which documentation files are relevant for
understanding Waterloo Docstrings, and which generated or auxiliary files
should usually be ignored.

Read first
==========

Read these files in this order:

1. source/index.rst
   Sphinx table of contents.

2. source/introduction.rst
   Project purpose, principles, normativity model, output formats.

3. source/format.rst
   Main specification. This is the most important file for implementation,
   validation, parsing, and rule-ID related work.

4. source/examples_minimax.rst
   Minimal and full docstring examples for modules, classes, functions,
   methods, and inherited methods.

5. source/examples.rst
   Additional examples: factories, properties, decorators, coroutines,
   definitions, inherited definitions, nested classes, free-form flow.

6. source/tools.rst
   waterlint and diagnostic/error-code reference.

7. source/json_io.rst
   JSON output format and LLM-readable documentation workflow.

8. source/html_output_layer.rst
   HTML5 rendering from Waterloo JSON.

Read examples selectively
=========================

When examples are referenced via literalinclude, read the corresponding file
under examples/. The most useful examples are:

- examples/test_docitem_module_minimal.py
- examples/test_docitem_module_full.py
- examples/test_docitem_class_minimal.py
- examples/test_docitem_class_full.py
- examples/test_docitem_function_minimal.py
- examples/test_docitem_function_medium.py
- examples/test_docitem_function_full.py
- examples/test_docitem_factory_vec2d.py
- examples/test_docitem_definitions_inherited.py
- examples/test_scope_mix.py
- examples/test_flow_control.py

Read only when needed
=====================

- source/reference.rst
  API reference entry points. Useful for finding documented functions/classes,
  but not the first place to learn the format.

- examples/pytest_bad_*.py
  Negative validator cases. Read only when working on validator diagnostics
  or a specific rule ID.

Usually ignore
==============

Do not read these unless the task explicitly concerns generated output,
schemas, rendering artifacts, or build/debug state:

- build/
- .mypy_cache/
- examples/__pycache__/
- output-html/
- output-json/
- examples/golden_files/
- img/
- input-html/
- input-json/
- input-python/
- source/_static/

Context note
============

The useful reST documentation is small compared to the whole doc directory.
The full package_main/doc directory includes generated output and caches, so
agents should not recursively ingest it without filtering.

Maintenance note
================

This project is still evolving. Update this file occasionally when major
documentation files, example groups, or generated-output directories are added,
removed, or renamed.
